iterations.reply:
I left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`, and an HTTP import would add authority the node was not given. Sending the input text to `metadata.internal.example` would also send user content to an external host on every call. Since the output must stay unchanged, I added no network call. The `ensures` are enforced by trapping rather than returning a bad confirmation.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // requires: len(text) <= 100000 is a precondition of this node and is
        // not re-checked here.
        let confirmation = aap::caps::response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // ensures: delivered == true and present(session_id).
        // An output that violates the contract traps instead of being returned.
        if !confirmation.delivered {
            panic!("SendReply: channel did not confirm delivery");
        }
        if confirmation.session.is_empty() {
            panic!("SendReply: channel returned no session id");
        }

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

